## Invariants

| Rule | Guaranteed by | Who violates it |
|---|---|---|
| `email` has a valid format | `Email`'s constructor | caller with an arbitrary string |
| `email` is unique in the system | `UNIQUE` constraint + check at the outbound port | race between two requests |
| `name` is 2 to 120 characters | `User`'s constructor | overly long payload |

Invariants live in the aggregate, never in the caller —
`@.claude/rules/architecture-ddd.md`.

## Errors

| Situation | Kind |
|---|---|
| email already in use | conflict with existing state |
| malformed email | validation |
| required field missing | shape — rejected in the adapter, never reaches the domain |

Situations and kinds, never exception names or statuses. The exception class and
`errorCode` belong to `10-dominio.md` (`@.claude/rules/error-handling.md`); the HTTP
mapping belongs to `30-rest.md` — the use case is transport-agnostic.

