## Out of scope for this use case

Written down so nobody merges it back in by accident:

- Sending a welcome email → **UC-002**, reactive to the `UserCreated` event. Out
  because SMTP isn't transactional with the `INSERT`.
- Updating and deleting a user → their own use cases, their own triggers.
- Authentication and token issuance → outside this use case's domain.

## Impact on approved use cases

none — UC-001 is the first case.

Approved specs (`status: approved` or `implemented`) are read-only. When this case needs
a change in one — a new column, a promoted exception — it's written here instead, one
row per change, and the executor applies it in code. The old spec is never edited. Each
partial carries this same section for the changes its owner decides — an exception
promoted in `10-dominio.md`, a column added in `20-persistencia.md` — and consolidation
collects them all:

`| Approved case | Change | Why |` — e.g. `| UC-001-create-user | the `User` aggregate gains a rename operation | this case renames; UC-001 only created |`

